{
 "summary": "Checkout failures (gateway 502) originate in inventory, where POST /reserve returns 500 alongside 'connection pool exhausted' errors; orders and gateway only pass that failure upstream. The orders 2.9.0 deploy landed about 30s before the first errors, but nothing in the evidence shows orders itself failing or changing how it calls inventory, so the deploy is a lead, not a confirmed cause.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Inventory exhausted its connection pool and returned 500 on POST /reserve. Orders surfaced this as 502, and gateway surfaced it as 502 on POST /checkout. What exhausted the pool is unknown. The orders 2.9.0 deploy is a timing correlate only.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-213f659d4a53",
   "ev-ca4a2a777123",
   "ev-c918d3739720",
   "ev-db030ea8939e",
   "ev-f623939438b5"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders was deployed from 2.7.0 to 2.9.0 at 00:32:40Z, about 31s before the first error traces and logs at 00:33:11Z. All 17 failing traces ran orders=2.9.0. However, all of them also ran gateway=1.4.2 and inventory=3.1.5, so the release tags do not single out orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-49e15e3b17b9",
    "ev-ca4a2a777123"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory's request rate averaged 1.38 req/s, the same as orders. The available metrics show no obvious traffic surge from orders that would explain pool exhaustion.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-f623939438b5",
    "ev-f0674321ffa2"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:32:40Z",
   "event": "Orders deployed 2.7.0 -> 2.9.0 by ci-pipeline.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-49e15e3b17b9"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:33:11Z",
   "event": "First failing checkout traces appear. Inventory logs 'connection pool exhausted', orders logs 'inventory reservation failed with status 500', and gateway logs 'checkout failed: orders returned 502'.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ca4a2a777123",
    "ev-213f659d4a53",
    "ev-c918d3739720",
    "ev-db030ea8939e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:33:39Z",
   "event": "Inventory and orders 5xx ratios reach 5% or higher.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-f623939438b5",
    "ev-f0674321ffa2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:34:09Z",
   "event": "Gateway 5xx ratio reaches 5% or higher.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-e16ccc0b3a7a"
   ]
  },
  {
   "time": "2026-10-24T00:35:37Z",
   "event": "Last observed failing trace and error logs; errors are still occurring at the end of the window.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ca4a2a777123",
    "ev-213f659d4a53"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Orders is not the origin of the errors. Its only error log reports a 500 received from inventory, and the trace error path ends at inventory POST /reserve (500).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-c918d3739720",
    "ev-ca4a2a777123"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "This is not a latency or timeout cascade. No service shows a p95 latency onset, p95 stayed low (inventory max 47ms, orders max 106ms, gateway max 196ms), and failing traces completed in 9-59ms.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-f623939438b5",
    "ev-f0674321ffa2",
    "ev-e16ccc0b3a7a",
    "ev-ca4a2a777123"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Gateway is not the origin. It only reports the 502 returned by orders.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-db030ea8939e",
    "ev-ca4a2a777123"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "Which resource inventory's connection pool fronts (e.g., a database) and what exhausted it; no database or pool-utilization metrics are in the snapshot.",
  "Whether orders 2.9.0 changed how it calls inventory (e.g., connection reuse, retries, concurrency). The deploy record has no changelog, and no per-caller connection counts are available.",
  "Whether the errors stop if orders is rolled back to 2.7.0.",
  "Whether anything else changed in inventory or its dependencies around 00:33Z; only the orders deploy is recorded."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Investigate inventory's connection pool: check pool size, active and idle connections, and the health of the backing datastore. Raise the pool limit or recycle connections if they are leaked.",
   "rationale": "Inventory's 'connection pool exhausted' errors coincide exactly with every failing request, and inventory is where the failure path ends.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-213f659d4a53",
    "ev-ca4a2a777123"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Review the orders 2.7.0 -> 2.9.0 diff for changes to inventory client behavior. If impact continues, roll orders back to 2.7.0 as a low-cost test.",
   "rationale": "The deploy preceded the errors by about 31s. A rollback would confirm or rule out orders 2.9.0 as the trigger of inventory's pool exhaustion.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-49e15e3b17b9",
    "ev-c918d3739720"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Inspect example traces 481f243affb4d174fa1e7acb824f08d7 and 2b21011a658b35f4c4cbc613aa3a272e for the inventory span details.",
   "rationale": "Both appear in the failing trace sample or log patterns and are linked to the pool-exhaustion errors in inventory.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ca4a2a777123",
    "ev-213f659d4a53"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
